WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:03.100
Today we look at two ways to display data.

2
00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:05.740
First a bar graph.

3
00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:10.460
This one shows the the proportion of TikTok users in each age group.

4
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:17.374
As you can see here the tallest bar is the 10 to 19 age group at about 32 and a half

5
00:00:17.374 --> 00:00:22.300
percent percent followed by 20 to 29 at 29 and a half percent.

6
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:32.028
After that the bars drop about 16% for 30 to 39 about 14% for 40 to 49 and 7% for 50

7
00:00:32.028 --> 00:00:33.100
and older.

8
00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:38.780
In a bar graph the bars stand for categories so they are separated by gaps.

9
00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:42.380
Next a histogram. histogram.

10
00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:47.084
A histogram is a graph of quantitative data in which the bars touch and each bar

11
00:00:47.084 --> 00:00:49.260
covers an covers an interval of values.

12
00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:54.847
Here the data are the number of of books bought by 50 part-time students at ABC

13
00:00:54.847 --> 00:00:55.340
College.

14
00:00:55.740 --> 00:01:01.387
The intervals run from one half to six and a half one book wide so there are six

15
00:01:01.387 --> 00:01:01.740
bars.

16
00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:08.758
three books is the most common answer with 16 students 11 students bought one book

17
00:01:08.758 --> 00:01:15.291
and 10 bought two I want to emphasize this the frequencies must add up to the number

18
00:01:15.291 --> 00:01:16.380
of students 50

19
00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:16.540
50

20
00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:19.580
always check that before you draw the histogram
